  "worked_solution": "First, let's consider the unit square spanned by the vectors $i$ and $j.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062085/assets/db15a65fd944c24ea2545baea08e6a0789b749295f623d8d4fdc2f07a37d4b73.png)\n\nNow, using the fact that $T(i)=i$ and $T(j)=1.5i+j,$ we can draw the image of the square under the transformation $T:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062085/assets/f5ebbff856529ad8cd3da41bf2f7d373294af3e0153c5e8da7da4c7b069b8b25.png)\n\nTherefore, the linear transformation $T$ represents a horizontal shear with a shear factor of $1.5.$",
